# Clean Code: Naming

## Choose descriptive and unambiguous names

```php
// BAD
$d = Carbon::now()->diffInDays($start);

// GOOD
$daysSinceCreation = Carbon::now()->diffInDays($createdAt);
```

## Make meaningful distinctions

```php
// BAD
function getUserInfo() {}
function getUserData() {}

// GOOD
function getUserProfile() {}
function getUserPermissions() {}
```

## Use pronounceable names

```php
// BAD
$ymdhms = now()->format('Y-m-d H:i:s');

// GOOD
$formattedTimestamp = now()->format('Y-m-d H:i:s');
```

## Use searchable names

```php
// BAD
if ($status === 3) { ... }

// GOOD
if ($status === OrderStatus::Completed) { ... }
```

## Replace magic numbers with named constants

```php
// BAD
$tax = $price * 0.11;

// GOOD
const TAX_RATE = 0.11;
$tax = $price * TAX_RATE;
```

## Avoid encodings and type prefixes

```php
// BAD
$strName = 'John';
$iAge = 25;
$arrItems = [];

// GOOD
$name = 'John';
$age = 25;
$items = [];
```

## Use explanatory variables for complex expressions

```php
// BAD
if (preg_match('/^(\d{4})-(\d{2})-(\d{2})$/', $input, $m)) {
    return Carbon::create($m[1], $m[2], $m[3]);
}

// GOOD
if (preg_match('/^(\d{4})-(\d{2})-(\d{2})$/', $input, $matches)) {
    [$fullMatch, $year, $month, $day] = $matches;
    return Carbon::create($year, $month, $day);
}
```

## Prefer dedicated value objects over primitives

```php
// BAD
function createOrder(string $email, float $amount, string $currency): void { ... }

// GOOD
function createOrder(Email $email, Money $amount): void { ... }
```
